<meta type=article>
  <title | Inline math and code spans in pipe-form content>
  <author | Test Author>
</meta>

<section | Inline math in pipe-form statement bodies>

A regression fixture for the bug-fix arc. LaTeX backslash commands written
inside inline math and inside code spans, when they appear in pipe-form
named-tag content, must survive the parser's escape processing. Before the
OpaqueSpan grammar rule the commands below produced visible parse-error
markers and the surrounding prose was swallowed into a broken math span.

<definition #def:closure | A set $S$ is closed under $\circ$ when $a \circ b \in S$ holds for all $a, b \in S$.>

<lemma #lem:sqrt | If $f(x) = \sqrt{x}$ then $f$ is defined for every $x \geq 0$.>

<remark | Throughout we write $\mathcal{O}(n \log n)$ for the asymptotic upper bound.>

<section | Display math and code spans in pipe-form content>

<aside | Euler connected five fundamental constants in a single line:

$$
e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0
$$

which remains striking for its economy.>

<aside | On Windows the build cache lives at `C:\Users\me\AppData\Local` by default.>

<aside | The linter flags a stray range with the double-backtick pattern ``\d+-\d+`` on each line.>
